  "sources": [
    {
      "source": "HOKFIRE",
      "url": "https://www.hokfire.com/",
      "field": "abilities",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "Passive",
          "name": "Serpent's Envoy",
          "desc": "Basic Attacks unleash serpent blades to deal damage, reducing Skill 1's cooldown for every enemy hit."
        },
        {
          "type": "Skill 1",
          "name": "Deadly Fang",
          "desc": "Activates a serpent blade and gains Movement Speed. She can quickly scale walls should she run into them during this period."
        },
        {
          "type": "Skill 2",
          "name": "Furtive Attack",
          "desc": "Summons the Fire Serpent at the target location, which then moves toward her, damaging and slowing enemies in its path. If serpent blades are active, it deals additional damage to enemies. If not, the cooldown is reduced."
        },
        {
          "type": "Ultimate",
          "name": "Blazing Glare",
          "desc": "Releases the Fire Serpent in the target direction, dealing damage and blinding enemies in its path, and gains a serpent blade. During this time, both attacking and being attacked will accumulate Fury. At full Fury, deals area damage and launches enemies."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "HOKFIRE",
      "url": "https://www.hokfire.com/",
      "field": "guide",
      "content": {
        "pros": [
          "Great Mobility",
          "Strong kiting",
          "Excellent DPS"
        ],
        "cons": [
          "Vulnerable to dives",
          "Weak early game",
          "Hard to chase enemies"
        ],
        "gameplay_tips": "## Early Game\nLuara's early game is very weak. With her low attack range, it's extremely difficult to walk up and try to trade efficiently, so most of the time you want to stay underneath the tower and farm safely. Start with Skill 2 to safely farm from range and try to poke the enemy at the same time. Skill 1 can help you clear minion waves and gives you extra movement speed to run out of the enemy Marksman's attack range and escape ganks.\n\n## Teamfights\nWith Luara's low range, it's always best to attack the first enemy in front of you. Always fight around terrain so you can use your Skill 1 to jump over walls to escape danger. Your Ultimate Blazing Glare is a game changer. It does insane damage, and blinding is a very strong tool to have, where enemies' attacks and skills will miss you. It's best to save this for when you get dove on by assassins\n\n## Tips & Tricks\nIn fights, stay near a wall so you can use Skill 1 to jump over and escape\nUse Skill 1 before Skill 2 to get a serpent blade that does damage when Skill 2 hits"
      }
    },
    {
      "source": "Kurohiko",
